      "math_academy_id": "q-158197",
      "sequence_position": 3,
      "problem": "Which of the following shaded regions corresponds to the domain of the function $g(x,y)=\\frac{1}{x-y}?$",
      "worked_solution": "The function is well-defined at all points $(x,y)$ for which the following condition is satisfied:\n\n- The expression in the denominator is not equal to zero.\n\nAs a result, the points in the domain must satisfy the following inequality:\n\n$$\nx-y\\ne 0\\,⟹\\,y\\ne x\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,y\\ne x}.\n$$\n\nSince the expression involves the $\\ne $ sign, the line is *not* part of the domain. Therefore, we draw the dashed line $y=x$ and shade *above* and *below* the line.\n\nThe resulting domain is as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14124092/assets/6953e2f817a786ae5ea52ea224a31b12a40a3ca89999a6bd5b1453eec11f8559.png)",
